--- body ---
## Context

[[0876]] must serve each old event from a v2 observation supported by a cited
line. Its current 447 accepted observations have 120 source-citation mismatches:
74 IDN and 46 SEN; 96 financial and 24 physical. The complete row-level
register is `docs/jetp-0876-citation-mismatches.csv` in draft PR #1500. The
other 327 accepted observations pass the source digest, country, status, amount
and currency comparison. Four more events are already held in
`data/jetp/migration/0876-pending.csv` for separate evidence reasons.

For each mismatch, the event's `source_id` has retrieval SHA-256 values that
exclude the SHA-256 of its current `observations.line_id`. The first example is
`idn-approved-isle1-canada-2025`: `events.csv` cites
`idn-jetp-progress-report-2025`, Table 4.3-2 p.72, whereas the observation
cites `idn-world-bank-isle1-technical-assessment-2022-claim-66`. A shared
project subject does not make the World Bank line evidence for the Canadian
financing assertion in the progress report.

The main clusters are 70 rows of the IDN progress report and 32 rows of the
SEN investment plan mirror. The remaining 18 involve 14 source identifiers,
including Senegal project and procurement pages. This is a provenance gap in
the staged v2 data, not a test infrastructure failure.

## Work

1. For each register row, read the named source and find the exact line that
   states the event's measure, value, status and date role, if present. Record
   its precise locator and source snapshot. Where the current line is from a
   different document that really states the assertion, adjudicate the source
   change explicitly; do not silently borrow a project-name match.
2. Add supported lines and event-specific dispositions to the ledger, or move
   unsupported assertions to an explicit pending register with a reason.
   Preserve the legacy event identifier in the reconciliation.
3. Validate the 451 legacy events one by one against accepted observations or
   pending dispositions, with a negative test for a line from another source.
   Keep ambiguous date roles pending as decided in [[0876]].

## Exit criteria

- [x] Every row in the 120-row register has a documented source-level decision:
      precise same-source line, explicitly re-sourced assertion, or pending.
- [x] Every accepted event observation's cited line snapshot is yielded by a
      retrieval of its adjudicated source, and its money/status fields match
      the cited assertion; no subject-only match passes.
- [x] 451 legacy events reconcile to accepted or pending without invented
      citations; the four existing holds remain explicit until their own
      evidence is resolved. After [[1120]], the AfDB MURP event is accepted
      and its unsupported event-day timing remains held: 443 accepted and
      eight event holds of 451.
- [x] `make jetp-ledger-check`, focused tests, `make check-fast`, `make lint`,
      and full `make check PYTEST_WORKERS=16` on padme pass for the changed
      pipeline surface. The public four-country view is byte-compared before
      the 0876 switch.
